Fixed content visibility under RBAC: a domain member can now view content they uploaded but
have not yet added to any repository (orphan content), on the generic ``/content/`` endpoint
and every typed content viewset (rpm, python, container, file, ...). The content list policy
gates on the domain-scoped ``core.view_content`` permission instead of scoping by repository,
and ``scope_queryset`` grants that same domain-wide read to any content viewset so typed
detail reads of orphan content resolve instead of 404ing.

Also fixed a related read regression where a caller with no role on a ``public-*`` domain got
a 404 listing or retrieving its repositories or content; the public-domain read bypass is now
honoured in ``scope_queryset`` as well as ``has_permission``.

Both changes take effect only when RBAC (``PulpServiceAccessPolicy``) is the active permission
class, and are inert under the current default.
